<title>INDIA: India's Saw Pipes 95/96 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's Saw Pipes 95/96 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end-June, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   470.5 vs   541.6</p>
<p>    Div (rupees)	   3.0 vs     3.0</p>
<p>    Gross sales	5,014.0 vs 3,479.8</p>
<p>    Other income	 108.9 vs   100.5</p>
<p>    Expenditure	4,072.7 vs 2,814.7</p>
<p>    Interest	     425.5 vs   160.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit	 624.7 vs   604.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 100.1 vs    63.0</p>
<p>    Tax		     54.1 vs     0.1</p>
<p>NOTE: Saw Pipes Ltd, a Jindal Organisation company, released the results in a statement. It said interest costs were higher mainly due to term loans for funding the Nashik Plant, where it said activity was quite low in its first year of operations.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom (91-11-301 2024)</p>
</text>
